    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d70">

                <pb facs="0150" n="984" xml:id="pg984"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 657.119/422</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Great Britain</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Page</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                        State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">London</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1918-04-23T18:00:00+01:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">April 23, 1918, 6 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                        <lb/> [<hi rendition="#italic">Received April 24, 3.25 a.m.</hi>]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>9673. War Trade Board [from Sheldon]:</p>
                <p>No. 471. Your 343, April 16, Department’s 7302, and your 375, April 22,
                    Department’s 7369.<anchor n="1" xml:id="d70-f1"/> British, French, and Italian
                    representatives are authorized to extend relaxation of embargo on nonessentials
                    to Norway and Denmark and only await your approval to determine date on which to
                    make same operative. Understand that possibility reopening negotiations with
                    representatives of Denmark might make it inadvisable extend relaxation to
                    Denmark at present but would inquire if you approve regarding Norway.<anchor
                        n="2" xml:id="d70-f2"/>
                </p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Page</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d70-f1" n="1" xml:id="d70-f1-content">
                <p>The latter not printed.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d70-f2" n="2" xml:id="d70-f2-content">
                <p>The reply of May 4, Department’s No. 7570, War Trade Board’s No. 428, states: “We
                    have approved the extension of the relaxation of the embargo on non-essentials
                    to Denmark. … Norway of course is not considered in this connection in view of
                    the recent conclusion of the agreement with her.” (File No. 657.119/422.)</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
